.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    Understand this assignment’s expectations — outcomes, activities, handbook, abilities, and how it connects to positions and other assignments — so coaching and check-ins stay grounded in a shared source of truth.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  = render "shared/maap/definition"
  %p.mb-3
    Assignments are the actionable job. Fresh, clear outcomes keep MAAP trustworthy. Anyone can propose edits; only people with update permission publish them.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Header
  %ul.mb-3
    %li
      The title dropdown switches among assignments, grouped by department and sorted alphabetically.
    %li The info icon expands this help.
    %li
      The
      %i.bi.bi-pencil
      button opens Edit Assignment when you have permission.
    %li Use the view switcher for Public / Organization / related management pages.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 What to look for
  %ul.mb-3
    %li Outcomes, required activities, and handbook describe what “good” looks like.
    %li Ability milestones and assignment reliance show how this work connects to skills and neighbors.
    %li
      %strong All proposed edits
      opens the queue of draft and submitted proposals for this assignment.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Example
  %p.mb-0.small.text-muted
    An assignment titled “Client Success Driver” with three outcomes and linked abilities is ready for expectation alignment. If outcomes feel stale, open All proposed edits or Propose edit to contribute without rewriting MAAP unilaterally.
